[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658995982","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3658995982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3658995982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aF9kO","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T06:11:17Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T06:11:17Z","body":"CC @bruvzg My guess is that this is happening on Betsy initialization. Betsy does check `can_create_rendering_device()`, but it must be returning true in this case, which means that `test_rd_creation` may not be detecting the problem on this device correctly. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658995982/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714245734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3714245734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3714245734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dYuRm","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T10:52:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T10:52:59Z","body":"@veganaiZe I expect this would still fail as your device might only support up to D3D11, but could you try setting the project setting `rendering/rendering_device/driver.windows` to `d3d12` in 4.6-beta2 or later, and see if this bug still happens?\n\nTo be clear if that fixes the crash, it wouldn't be a solution per se as we still need to figure out the Vulkan crash, but it might show how widespread the bug might be in the future (as we're making D3D12 the default on Windows in 4.6 for new projects).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714245734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714269953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3714269953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3714269953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dY0MB","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T11:00:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T11:00:43Z","body":"`can_create_rendering_device` check is always trying to use Vulkan first and then fallbacks to DX12, project setting probably won't have any effect. But technically, this GPU should support both.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714269953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714325479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3714325479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3714325479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dZBvn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T11:18:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T11:18:25Z","body":"> `can_create_rendering_device` check is always trying to use Vulkan first and then fallbacks to DX12, project setting probably won't have any effect.\n\nI wonder if we should swap that logic now that we're making D3D12 the default driver for new projects?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714325479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714360810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3714360810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3714360810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dZKXq","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T11:30:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T11:30:21Z","body":"BetsyCompressor and Lightmaapper, do not have code for DX12 at all, only Metal and Vulkan, so it is quite inconsistent and would make sense to either follow same OS defaults or use project setting. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714360810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714464481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3714464481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3714464481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dZjrh","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T12:06:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T12:06:43Z","body":"> Godot v4.5.1.stable - Windows Unknown (build 9600) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL ES 3/ANGLE (Compatibility) - ANGLE (AMD, AMD Radeon HD 8400 / R3 Series (0x00009830) Direct3D11 vs_5_0 ps_5_0, D3D11-21.19.407.0) - AMD A6-5200 APU with Radeon(TM) HD Graphics (4 threads) - 15.45 GiB memory\n\n@veganaiZe Could you share more details on what Windows version you're running (see e.g. `winver` command).\nIt seems like Godot couldn't detect it, and it reports build 9600 which would be Windows 8.1 which Godot 4.5 and 4.6 don't support.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714464481/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715691980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3715691980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3715691980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dePXM","user":{"login":"veganaiZe","id":7102064,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDIwNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7102064?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe","html_url":"https://github.com/veganaiZe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T17:51:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T17:52:16Z","body":"> I expect this would still fail as your device might only support up to D3D11, but could you try setting the project setting `rendering/rendering_device/driver.windows` to `d3d12` in 4.6-beta2 or later, and see if this bug still happens?\n\n@akien-mga Godot only works with ANGLE, in compatibility mode, against my Windows drivers.  (Even though, technically speaking, my drivers support OpenGL 4.5 / Vulkan 1.0)\n\n> Could you share more details on what Windows version you're running (see e.g. `winver` command). It seems like Godot couldn't detect it, and it reports build 9600 which would be Windows 8.1 which Godot 4.5 and 4.6 don't support.\n\n@akien-mga Yes, it's Windows 8.1 (x64) which Godot 4.5 / 4.6 seem to (unofficially) support.  Godot 4.5, for instance, works perfectly fine otherwise, from my experience, on Windows 8.1.  It's worth noting Windows 8.1 doesn't support DX12, of course.\n\n> `can_create_rendering_device` check is always trying to use Vulkan first and then fallbacks to DX12, project setting probably won't have any effect. But technically, this GPU should support both.\n\n@bruvzg Shouldn't it check for ANGLE first, regardless of Windows version?  (That's the driver Godot has me using.)\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715691980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715717159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3715717159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3715717159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7deVgn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T17:59:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T17:59:13Z","body":"> > `can_create_rendering_device` check is always trying to use Vulkan first and then fallbacks to DX12, project setting probably won't have any effect. But technically, this GPU should support both.\n> \n> [@bruvzg](https://github.com/bruvzg) Shouldn't it check for ANGLE first, regardless of Windows version? (That's the driver Godot has me using.)\n\nWhat's happening here is that even though you are using OpenGL / Compatibility via ANGLE, Godot has a feature to use a Vulkan or Direct3D 12 rendering context from an OpenGL editor for some specific operations such as texture compression on the GPU, and lightmap baking. In your case it's the texture compression that attempts to initialize a Vulkan context and crashes.\n\nThe way it's done is that there's a test to see whether Vulkan can be used on your device, and this test seems to wrongly pass on your device, but then when it's attempted for real, it crashes.\n\n---\n\n@clayjohn @bruvzg It's not a complete solution, but given how many edge cases we've had with the RD creation test over the past few releases, would it make sense to add an editor setting to disable the RD-dependent features in Compatibility (i.e. not attempt testing if it's supported)?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715717159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715723383","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3715723383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3715723383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7deXB3","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T18:00:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T18:00:38Z","body":"> Shouldn't it check for ANGLE first, regardless of Windows version?\n\nGPU compression only works with Vulkan/DX/Metal, but not with OpenGL (native or ANGLE). So if you try to import it, it is:\n- spawning another copy of Godot that is initializing both GL and Vulkan to check if it won't crash (with some low quality drivers do), and Vulkan can be initialized.\n- if the spawned process returns successfully, Vulkan content is initialized in the main process as well and used to compress textures. \n\nSo it might be the issue with ANGLE, since spawned process check always init native GL, it probably should be updated to use same logic to select ANGLE.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715723383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715742661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3715742661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3715742661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7debvF","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T18:06:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T18:06:02Z","body":"> It's not a complete solution, but given how many edge cases we've had with the RD creation test over the past few releases, would it make sense to add an editor setting to disable the RD-dependent features in Compatibility (i.e. not attempt testing if it's supported)?\n\n`rendering/textures/vram_compression/compress_with_gpu` already exist, not sure about lightmapper.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715742661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715834699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114067#issuecomment-3715834699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114067","id":3715834699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7deyNL","user":{"login":"veganaiZe","id":7102064,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDIwNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7102064?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/veganaiZe","html_url":"https://github.com/veganaiZe","followers_u